#DESCRIPTION
Hybrid PIC (kinetic ions / fluid electrons) parallel whistler-Alfven wave test.
Full generalized Ohm's law: convection + Hall + resistive (eta*J) + electron
pressure gradient (grad Pe / (e n_e)) terms ALL active, in normalized CGS units.

Parameters match the whistler test (same ion-scale normalization, uNormSI =
speed of light = v_A, so d_i ~ v_A ~ 1 in code units).  Here RESISTIVITY and
ELECTRONTEMPERATURE are enabled so the
complete Ohm's-law field solver is exercised.  The resistivity is dynamically
active (see the RESISTIVITY note below): it measurably reduces the late-time
transverse amplitude.  The electron pressure gradient acts on the (weak)
charge-density fluctuations produced by particle noise; the test is a
STABILITY / no-blow-up regression check for the full solver, not a dispersion
measurement.

#INITFROMSWMF
F                       initFromSWMF

#GEOMETRY
-3.2                    xMin  [code units; Lx = 6.4 d_i]
 3.2                    xMax
-0.05                   yMin
 0.05                   yMax
-0.05                   zMin
 0.05                   zMax

#NCELL
64                      nCellX
1                       nCellY
1                       nCellZ

#MAXBLOCKSIZE
64                      maxBlockSizeX
1                       maxBlockSizeY
1                       maxBlockSizeZ

#PERIODICITY
T                       isPeriodicX
T                       isPeriodicY
T                       isPeriodicZ

#SOLVEEM
F                       solveEM

#HYBRIDPIC
T                       useHybridPIC

Resistive term ON. Converted internally to code units
(etaCode = 4*pi*etaSI*Si2NoV*Si2NoL ~ 2.51 here). For the seeded n=1 mode the
discrete ohmic decay rate is (etaCode/4*pi)*sin^2(k*dx)/dx^2 ~ 0.19, i.e. ~70%
over the run; the measured net effect is smaller (~25% reduction of the
late-time transverse amplitude, see validate.py) because the kinetic-ion
response keeps re-exciting the field. Resistive CFL number
eta*kmax^2*dt_sub/(4*pi) = 1.2, below the 2.0 guard.
#RESISTIVITY
2.0e9                   etaResistivity  [m^2/s, SI magnetic diffusivity]

Electron-pressure-gradient term ON (isothermal, gamma = 1). Converted
internally to code units (TeCode = TeEV*e/(mp*uNormSI^2) ~ 0.19 here).
#ELECTRONTEMPERATURE
20.0                    electronTemperature  [eV]
1.0                     electronGamma
1.0                     electronDensity0

Sub-cycle the B update. The explicit Hall advance is limited by the discrete
grid-scale whistler mode, omega_max * dt_sub < S (S ~ 2.83 for RK4). Because the
compact curl operators (curl_center_to_node / curl_node_to_center) annihilate
the exact Nyquist mode and are far less stiff than the continuum estimate, the
effective omega_max here is ~100/Omega_i, so even dt = 0.02 is within the RK4
limit and nBSubcycle = 1 is stable (verified: the measured whistler frequency
is identical for nBSubcycle in {1,4,8,16,32}). nBSubcycle = 4 is chosen here
(verified stable, whistler frequency identical to {1,8,16,32}); it is sufficient
and provides a meaningful sub-cycling test without over-subcycling (4x cheaper
than the previous 32). The resistive and
electron-pressure-gradient terms are diffusive/stabilizing and do not stiffen
the Hall update, so this rationale is unchanged from the Hall-only whistler
case.
#BSUBCYCLE
4                       nBSubcycle

Single kinetic ion species (q = m = 1); the electron is an implicit
neutralizing massless fluid, so no electron particle species is present.
#PLASMA
1                       nSpecies
1.0                     mass
1.0                     charge

#UNIFORMSTATE
5.0                     rho [amu/cc]   Species 0: ions (n = 5 /cc)
0.0                     ux [km/s]
0.0                     uy [km/s]
0.0                     uz [km/s]
10000.0                 T [K]
1.0439e-8               bx [T]       uniform guide field Bx0 (B_code ~ 1)
0.0                     by [T]
0.0                     bz [T]
0.0                     ex [V/m]
0.0                     ey [V/m]
0.0                     ez [V/m]

#TESTCASE
HybridWave

#TIMESTEPPING
T                       useFixedDt
0.02                    dt

#NORMALIZATION
1.0e5                   lNormSI   [m]  ~ d_i so d_i ~ 1 in code units
1.0e5                   uNormSI   [m/s] tNorm = 1 s; sets cLight_SI = uNormSI

#MONITOR
50                      dnReport

#SAVELOG
1                       dnSavePic
1                       dnSavePT

#PARTICLES
2000                    nParticle per cell in X
1                       nParticle per cell in Y
1                       nParticle per cell in Z

#COMOVING
F                       solvePartInCoMov
0                       nSmoothBackGroundU

#UPWINDE
F                       useUpwindE
0.0                     limiterThetaE

#UPWINDB
F                       doSmoothB
0.0                     theta

#SAVEPLOT
1                       nPlot
z=0 fluid ascii pic     plotString
-1                      dn
6.25                    dt
1                       dx
Bx By Bz Ex Ey Ez       varName

#STOP
-1                      MaxIter
6.25                    TimeMax   ~0.5 whistler period (resistive damping)

#RUN

#AVGFIELDB
T                       useAvgFieldB
20                      nAvgFieldB
